engine.py adapts the upstream package's onnx_backend.py, stream.py and
audio.py. Changes: minimal NumPy/ONNX Runtime dependencies; managed model
paths and configurable CPU threads; per-node explicit recurrent state;
causal left padding, four-hop spectral delay compensation, exact-length
EOS draining and media-aligned dry/wet mixing. See provenance.json.
runtime.py and package declarations implement the ObliviousMic Module API.
This module is an independent integration, not an endorsement by Ceva-IP.

NumPy (BSD-3-Clause) and ONNX Runtime (MIT) are external runtime dependencies;
their code is not bundled in this module archive.
